 "title": "Spinal cord or root: upper motor neuron signs below a sensory level mean the cord, and which tracts are lost (corticospinal, spinothalamic, dorsal columns) sorts anterior, posterior, central and Brown-Sequard cord syndromes; a lower motor neuron pattern means the roots, either cauda equina (an emergency) or a single radiculopathy; each column gives the tracts hit, the presentation and the causes",
